  "id": "Compound::DB01093 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Dimethyl sulfoxide (DMSO) is shown to interact with Cyp3a4, a cytochrome P450 enzyme, and this interaction is linked to the participation of Cyp3a4 in metabolic processes that ultimately involve Cyp2c19. The evidence suggests that DMSO may modulate Cyp3a4's function, which in turn affects the activity of Cyp2c19. This mechanism is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that DMSO binds to Cyp3a4 and that this binding leads to a participation in metabolic pathways that are associated with Cyp2c19. The overlapping roles of Cyp3a4 in different metabolic processes, such as steroid hydroxylase activity and oxidoreductase activity, suggest that DMSO may influence Cyp2c19 through a common intermediary. The integrated evidence implies that DMSO could act as a modulator of Cyp2c19 activity by influencing Cyp3a4, though the exact nature of this modulation remains to be fully elucidated. The observed scores indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the mechanistic details.",
